Object.assign(TTD,{
"出车位前看了左边、打了灯，慢慢挪到车道边先左右看；车道里让了行人和车；车头停到大路边，左右看清楚，等到安全的空档才左转上大路，做得很好。": "You looked left and signalled before pulling out, crept to the edge of the aisle and looked both ways, yielded to pedestrians and cars in the aisle, brought the front up to the road edge, looked both ways and turned left onto the road only in a safe gap — well done.",
"进停车场前打了右转灯、让了行人；左转进车道前打了灯、让了对面的车；找车位前看镜、打灯，看了左边盲点，一次开进车位正中间，车身摆正、和两边的车对齐，挂 P、拉手刹，做得很好。": "You signalled right and yielded to pedestrians entering the lot, signalled and yielded to the oncoming car before turning left into the aisle, checked the mirror, signalled and checked the left blind spot before the spot, drove into the middle of it in one go, straight and lined up with the cars beside you, then shifted to P and set the parking brake — well done.",
"停车压到了停车线": "Stopped over the stop line",
"有停车线时，车头要停在粗白停车线后面，不要压线，更不能停到人行横道上。": "When there is a stop line, stop with the front of the car behind the thick white line — not on it, and certainly not on the crosswalk.",
"车头要停在接近停车线的地方（1～2 米内）。停得太远，别的车看不出你已经停好在等。": "Stop with the front of the car close to the stop line (within 1–2 m). Stopping too far back, other drivers can't tell you have stopped and are waiting.",
"停牌路口必须在停车线前完全停住（车速为 0）。慢慢滑过去（rolling stop）在路考里是严重错误。": "You must come to a complete stop (speed 0) before the stop line at a stop sign. Rolling through (a rolling stop) is a major error on the road test.",
"右转没有打转向灯": "No signal for the right turn",
"到停牌路口前（约 30 米）就要打右转灯，停车、观察、转弯的整个过程都开着。": "Signal right before reaching the stop sign (about 30 m before), and keep it on through the stop, the check and the turn.",
"右转灯要在停车之前就打好（离路口约 30 米）。": "Put the right signal on before you stop (about 30 m before the intersection).",
"（红圈是比你晚到的车：你先停稳，应该你先走。你一直不走，它只好先走了）": "(The red circle marks the car that arrived after you: you stopped first, so it was your turn. You didn't go, so it had to go first.)",
"（红圈是那位行人）": "(The red circle marks the pedestrian.)",
"（红圈是那辆比你先停下的车）": "(The red circle marks the car that stopped before you.)"
});
Object.assign(TTD,{
"严重": "Major",
"扣分项": "Deduction",
"驾驶总结": "Driving summary",
"灯变黄时停在了停车线后面，等横向绿灯过去，左转箭头亮了再左转，处理正确。": "You stopped behind the stop line when the light turned amber, waited for the cross traffic's green to finish, and turned left on the arrow — well handled.",
"进入路口等候，看清对面车流、右转车和行人，空档足够再转，绿灯左转处理得很好。": "You entered the intersection to wait, watched the oncoming traffic, right-turners and pedestrians, and turned when the gap was big enough — a well-handled green-light left turn.",
"灯变黄时你离停车线还有足够距离，停在了停车线后面，处理正确。": "When the light turned amber you still had room to stop, and you stopped behind the stop line — well handled.",
"你一直没有完成左转。": "You never completed the left turn.",
"考试中不提示对错，全部结束后统一给出结果。": "No feedback during the test — results are given at the end.",
"5 个路口全部处理正确，非常好！": "All 5 intersections handled correctly — excellent!",
"这一趟没有违规或危险驾驶，右转处理得很好。": "No violations or dangerous driving this run — a well-handled right turn.",
"提早换进最右的出口车道，换过去后跟上车流加速，快到出口才减速，进匝道弯道时车速合适，做得很好。": "You moved into the rightmost exit lane early, kept up with traffic after the change, slowed down only near the exit, and took the ramp curve at the right speed — well done.",
"提前换到右车道进入匝道，在加速车道里提速、找空档，打灯、看后视镜、看盲点后顺利并入高速，做得很好。": "You moved into the right lane early to take the ramp, sped up in the acceleration lane while looking for a gap, and merged smoothly after signalling and checking the mirror and blind spot — well done.",
"打灯、看后视镜、回头看盲区、找够空档再换线，两次换线都做得很好。": "Signal, mirror, shoulder check, wait for a big enough gap, then change — both lane changes were well done.",
"完全停车、看清左边、找到空档再转，红灯右转处理得很好。": "Full stop, a clear look left, and a turn only once there was a gap — a well-handled right turn on red.",
"你一直没有转弯。红灯右转不是必须的，看不清或没有把握时可以等绿灯；但路考时考官通常希望你在安全的空档里完成右转。": "You never turned. A right turn on red isn't required — if you can't see or aren't sure, you may wait for the green; but on the road test the examiner usually expects you to make the turn in a safe gap.",
"在人行横道前完全停车，看了左右，让比你先停下的车先走，轮到你时打着右转灯果断右转，做得很好。": "You stopped fully before the crosswalk, looked left and right, let the cars that stopped before you go first, and turned right decisively with your signal on when it was your turn — well done.",
"提前打灯，在人行横道前完全停车，看清左右（看不清时前移再看），找到两边都安全的空档果断左转，做得很好。": "You signalled early, stopped fully before the crosswalk, looked left and right (creeping forward when you couldn't see), and turned left decisively in a gap that was safe both ways — well done.",
"停车位置、后视镜、起步加速都做得很好。": "Stopping position, mirror checks and acceleration were all well done.",
"车速稳、后视镜和路口观察都做到了。": "Steady speed, and you did the mirror and intersection checks.",
"停在参考车旁边的位置准确，倒车时一直做 360° 观察，打方向的时机准确，没有碰车、没有碰路缘，停在车位中间、离路缘 30 厘米内，做得很好。": "You stopped in the right place beside the reference car, kept doing 360° checks while backing, steered at the right moments, touched neither car nor curb, and finished in the middle of the space within 30 cm of the curb — well done.",
"坡道停车、三点调头、平行停车都做得很好：每一步之前都做了观察、打了灯，停车位置准确。": "Hill parking, the three-point turn and parallel parking were all well done: you checked and signalled before every step and stopped in the right places.",
"打灯、右侧观察后靠边，没有挡住车道口；车轮方向正确，松刹车让车轮抵住路缘后挂 P；离开前打左灯、左侧观察，做得很好。": "You signalled and did a right-side check before pulling over, didn't block a driveway, turned the wheels the right way, let the wheel rest against the curb before shifting to P, and signalled left and did a left-side check before leaving — well done.",
"起始位置准确，倒车前做了 360° 观察，往右打到底、和旁边的车平行时回正，车停在车位正中间、车身摆正，挂 P、拉手刹，做得很好。": "Good starting position, a 360° check before backing, full right lock, straightened when parallel to the cars beside you, stopped straight in the middle of the spot, shifted to P and set the parking brake — well done.",
"靠边停在 30 厘米内，每一步之前都做了 M.S.B.，倒车回头看，没有原地打方向、没有碰路缘，三步完成调头，做得很好。": "You pulled over within 30 cm, did M.S.B. before every step, looked back while backing, didn't steer while stopped or touch the curb, and turned around in three steps — well done."
});
/* 错误的说明（总结卡片里每条错误下面那段话） */
Object.assign(TTD,{
"出车位前：看后视镜、打左转灯、转头看左边（按看左），确认没有车和行人再起步。": "Before pulling out: check the mirror, signal left and turn your head to look left (hold Look Left). Make sure there are no cars or pedestrians before moving off.",
"起步之前就要打好转向灯（要往哪边转就打哪边）。": "Signal before you start moving (signal the way you are going to turn).",
"按住前移慢慢往前挪，车头出到车道边时停一下，看左、看右看清车道，确认没有车、没有人再点行驶。": "Hold Creep to inch forward. Stop when the front of the car reaches the edge of the aisle, look left and right along the aisle, and only press Drive once there are no cars or people.",
"出车位时车道上有车开过来，它有路权：先停住让它过去，再出来。": "A car was coming along the aisle as you pulled out. It has the right-of-way: stop, let it pass, then pull out.",
"那辆车过去时你正好停着，但它过来之前你没有左右看车道。出车位前一定要左右看。": "You happened to be stopped when that car passed, but you didn't look left and right along the aisle before it came. Always look both ways before pulling out of a spot.",
"停车场里行人常常从车中间走出来横过车道：看到就停下让他走过去。": "In a parking lot, pedestrians often step out from between cars to cross the aisle. When you see one, stop and let them cross.",
"看到车尾的白色倒车灯亮了、车在往外倒，就要停下等它倒出来。它倒车时很难看到你。它还没倒进你要走的车道、或者停下来等你时，你可以慢慢开过去；它正往你前面的车道里倒，你还往前开，就算没有让行。": "White reverse lights on means the car is backing out — stop and wait for it. A reversing driver can hardly see you. If it hasn't backed into your path yet, or it has stopped to wait for you, you may creep past; if it is backing into the aisle ahead of you and you keep going, you failed to yield.",
"听到考官说右转，就要自己打右转灯，转完再关。": "When the examiner says turn right, put your right signal on yourself and turn it off after the turn.",
"车道尽头接上横着的通道：转弯前看左、看右（按住看左、看右）。通道上有车过来就停下让它；没有车就慢慢转过去，不用停。": "The aisle ends at a cross aisle: look left and right before turning (hold Look Left / Look Right). If a car is coming along it, stop and let it pass; if not, turn slowly without stopping.",
"往出口开的时候就要打好左转灯。": "Put your left signal on as you head toward the exit.",
"车道尽头接上横着的通道：左边（商铺前面）开过来的车在通道上直行，你要转进去，先停下让它过去。转弯前看左、看右。": "The aisle ends at a cross aisle: a car coming from the left (in front of the stores) is going straight along it, and you are turning in. Stop and let it pass first. Look left and right before turning.",
"出口要横过人行道：有行人在走，停在人行道前面让他先过。": "The exit crosses a sidewalk: if a pedestrian is walking, stop before the sidewalk and let them cross first.",
"出口没有停牌，但你没有路权：车头要停到大路边上（靠近路边石的位置），两边才看得远。停得太靠后，要再往前挪一点、停住再看。": "There is no stop sign at the exit, but you don't have the right-of-way: bring the front of the car up to the edge of the road (near the curb) so you can see far both ways. If you stop too far back, creep forward, stop and look again.",
"车头停到大路边以后，看左、看右、再看左，确认两个方向都有足够的空档再转。": "Once the front of the car is at the edge of the road, look left, right and left again, and make sure both directions have a big enough gap before turning.",
"你没有路权：要等两个方向都有足够的空档。左边过来的车（你要横过它的车道）至少要 3 秒以上，右边过来的车（你要并进它的车道）要更远。": "You don't have the right-of-way: wait for a big enough gap both ways. Cars from the left (whose lane you cross) need to be at least 3 seconds away; cars from the right (whose lane you join) need to be farther.",
"左转前一定要打左转灯，一般在停车线前约 30 米就打开。": "Always signal before a left turn, usually about 30 m before the stop line.",
"离停车线不到 15 米才打左转灯，后车和对面的车来不及反应。": "You signalled left less than 15 m from the stop line — too late for the cars behind and oncoming cars to react.",
"在路口里等候左转时，车身要摆正、车轮朝正前方。你停下来时车头已经往左歪了（车轮已经打了方向），如果被后车追尾，会被推进对面的车流。不要提前开始转弯，停在路口里车正轮正地等。": "While waiting in the intersection to turn left, keep the car straight with the wheels pointing forward. Your car had already angled left (the wheels were turned) when you stopped; if you were rear-ended you would be pushed into oncoming traffic. Don't start the turn early — wait in the intersection with the car and wheels straight.",
"路口里没有对面直行车、右转车，也没有行人过马路，没有任何需要让行的，应该直接转过去。你停下来超过 3 秒，后车按喇叭了。": "There were no oncoming through cars, no right-turners and no pedestrians crossing — nothing to yield to, so you should have turned straight away. You stopped for more than 3 seconds and the car behind honked.",
"你是第一辆左转车，绿灯时应该开过停车线，进入路口里等候（车头大约在路口中间前面，车轮朝正前方）。停在停车线后面等，会延误后面的车，也更难找到空档。": "You are the first left-turner: on a green light, drive past the stop line and wait inside the intersection (front of the car a little before the middle, wheels straight). Waiting behind the stop line delays the cars behind you and makes it harder to find a gap.",
"一次只能有一辆左转车在路口里等候。前面已经有车在路口里等左转时，你要停在停车线后面，等它转走了再开进路口。": "Only one left-turner may wait inside the intersection at a time. When a car ahead is already waiting there to turn left, stop behind the stop line and enter only after it has turned.",
"左转前要按“观察路口”看一眼左边——你要转入那条路的人行横道上有没有行人，再确认对面车流的空档。": "Before turning left, press Check Intersection to look left — check for pedestrians on the crosswalk of the road you are turning into — then confirm the gap in oncoming traffic.",
"对面直行车的空档不够你就转了。左转要让对面直行车：两条车道都要看，要等到两条车道都有足够的空档（你能在对面车到达之前完全转过去）再转。": "You turned without a big enough gap in oncoming traffic. A left turn must yield to oncoming through traffic: watch both lanes and wait until both have a gap big enough for you to finish the turn before the oncoming cars arrive.",
"对面在路口里等的左转车已经先开始转了，它的路线会从你车头前经过。要等它转过你的车头再走，否则两车会撞上。": "The oncoming left-turner waiting in the intersection had already started turning, and its path crosses in front of you. Wait until it has passed your front before going, or the two cars will collide.",
"对面有车打着右转灯，要转进你要去的同一条路。对面右转车比你优先，要等它转完（或者确认它停下来让行人），两车不要同时转进同一条路。": "An oncoming car is signalling right to turn into the same road you are going to. The oncoming right-turner has priority: wait until it has turned (or you are sure it has stopped for pedestrians). Don't turn into the same road at the same time.",
"对面自行车道里有自行车直行过来。自行车和对面直行车一样有路权，要等它过去再转。": "A cyclist is coming straight through in the oncoming bike lane. Cyclists have the same right-of-way as oncoming through cars — wait for it to pass before turning.",
"你要转入那条路的人行横道上有行人正在过（或者正要从你这一侧走过来）。左转要先确认能让行人、同时对面直行车有空档，两样都满足才转；有行人就在路口里原地等。": "Pedestrians are crossing (or about to cross from your side) on the crosswalk of the road you are turning into. Only turn when you can yield to the pedestrians and there is also a gap in oncoming traffic; if there are pedestrians, wait where you are in the intersection.",
"你已经开始转弯，却停在了对面的车道上，挡住了对面直行车，非常危险，也会堵塞交通。开始转之前就要确认行人和对面车流都允许你一次转过去。": "You had started turning but stopped in the oncoming lanes, blocking oncoming traffic — very dangerous, and it jams traffic. Before you start the turn, make sure the pedestrians and oncoming traffic will let you turn in one go.",
"你已经完全进了路口、在待转位置等候，灯变黄、变红后，对面的车停下来了，你应该在安全时尽快完成左转、清空路口。停在路口里不走，会挡住横向的车。": "You were fully in the intersection, waiting to turn. After the light turned amber then red and oncoming traffic stopped, you should have finished the left turn as soon as it was safe and cleared the intersection. Staying there blocks the cross traffic.",
"黄灯、红灯时要停在停车线后面。稍微过了线、车头还没进人行横道，就停在那里等下一个绿灯（不要倒车），不算严重错误，但要注意提早减速。": "On amber or red, stop behind the stop line. If you are slightly over the line but not yet in the crosswalk, stay there for the next green (don't back up). It isn't a major error, but brake earlier next time.",
"黄灯、红灯时车头进了人行横道，会挡住过马路的行人。就停在那里等下一个绿灯（不要倒车），下次要提早减速、停在停车线后面。": "On amber or red, the front of your car went into the crosswalk and blocks crossing pedestrians. Stay there for the next green (don't back up), and next time slow down earlier and stop behind the stop line.",
"灯变黄时你离停车线还有足够的距离，能安全停下，就应该停在停车线后面，不要再开进路口。": "When the light turned amber you still had enough room to stop safely, so you should have stopped behind the stop line instead of entering the intersection.",
"红灯时越过了停车线。": "You crossed the stop line on a red light.",
"箭头变黄时你离停车线还有足够的距离，能安全停下。本方圆灯是红灯，箭头一熄灭就不能再左转，应该停在停车线后面，等圆灯变绿再按绿灯左转的方法进路口等候。": "When the arrow turned amber you still had enough room to stop safely. Your round light is red, and once the arrow goes off you can no longer turn left. Stop behind the stop line and wait for the round light to turn green, then enter and wait as in a green-light left turn.",
"左转箭头是绿灯，这时左转有保护（对面直行车是红灯），应该跟着前车顺畅地转过去。停着不走会延误后面的车，还可能错过箭头。": "The left-turn arrow is green, so your turn is protected (oncoming traffic has a red light). Follow the car ahead and turn smoothly. Sitting still delays the cars behind you and you may miss the arrow.",
"你的车和其他车辆撞上了。没有让行、抢着转弯，就会造成碰撞，路考立即结束。": "Your car collided with another vehicle. Not yielding and forcing the turn causes collisions — the road test ends immediately.",
"你的车撞到了正在过马路的行人。": "Your car hit a pedestrian who was crossing the road.",
"你的车撞到了对面骑过来的自行车。": "Your car hit an oncoming cyclist.",
"左转要转进最近的左车道；转完以后不用等考官说，自己在安全时（打右转灯、看后视镜、回头看右边盲点）换到右车道。左车道是超车道，一直占着会挡住后面要超车的车。考官等了一会儿你还没换，就会提醒你，这要扣分。": "Turn into the nearest (left) lane; after the turn, don't wait for the examiner — when it's safe, move into the right lane yourself (signal right, check the mirror, look over your right shoulder). The left lane is the passing lane; staying in it blocks cars that want to pass. If the examiner has to remind you after a while, you lose marks.",
"换到右车道前要先打右转灯，闪几下再换。": "Signal right before moving into the right lane, and let it flash a few times before you change.",
"打了转向灯要闪几下（约 2 秒以上），让后面的车看到，再开始换。": "Let the signal flash a few times (about 2 seconds or more) so the cars behind can see it, then start the lane change.",
"换车道前要看后视镜，确认后面和右后方的车离得够远。": "Check the mirror before changing lanes to make sure the cars behind and to the right rear are far enough away.",
"后视镜看不到右后方的盲区：换车道前要回头看一眼右边盲点。": "Mirrors can't see the blind spot to your right rear: look over your right shoulder before changing lanes.",
"右后方的车正在开过来（或者就在你旁边的盲区里），你换过去会逼它急刹车，甚至撞上。要等它超过去、右车道有足够空档再换。": "A car was coming up on your right rear (or was right beside you in the blind spot). Moving over would force it to brake hard or even cause a crash. Wait until it has passed and the right lane has enough room.",
"换好车道后要关掉转向灯，不然后面的车会以为你还要再换。": "Turn your signal off after the lane change, or the cars behind will think you are changing lanes again.",
"对面的左转车在你进入路口的同时启动了。它通常转入左侧车道，你转入右侧车道，两车会肩并肩同时进入路口，这是应避免的危险时刻。错在抢行的它，但你看到它启动后，只有确认能错开进入路口才可以继续，否则要先停车让它先转。": "The oncoming left-turner started moving just as you entered the intersection. It usually turns into the left lane and you into the right lane, so both cars enter side by side — a dangerous moment to avoid. It is the one in the wrong for forcing its way, but once you see it start, only continue if you are sure you can enter at a different moment; otherwise stop and let it turn first.",
"路口明确没有冲突，你停着不走，后方车辆鸣笛了。看清之后应马上行驶：等右转走开的行人要在 2 秒内走，其余情况 3 秒内。": "The intersection was clearly free of conflicts, but you stayed stopped and the car behind honked. Once you've checked, go straight away: within 2 seconds after the pedestrians walk clear, within 3 seconds otherwise.",
"对面在路口里等着左转的是一辆警车，但它没有闪灯、没有鸣笛，不是在执行紧急任务，就按普通车对待：你有路权，直接转，不用让它。你停了超过 3 秒，后方鸣笛了。": "The car waiting to turn left across from you was a police car, but without lights or siren it isn't on an emergency call — treat it like any other car. You have the right-of-way, so turn without yielding to it. You stopped for more than 3 seconds and the car behind honked.",
"对面的左转车在等你，你有路权，不用让它。路口明确没有冲突，你停了超过 3 秒，后方鸣笛，对面的车也趁机转走了。": "The oncoming left-turner was waiting for you — you have the right-of-way and don't need to yield to it. The intersection was clearly free of conflicts; you stopped for more than 3 seconds, the car behind honked, and the oncoming car took the chance to turn.",
"你右边的自行车道里有一辆自行车在追上来，你转弯前没有看中镜、右镜和右后盲区，就向右切进了自行车道。这是右转车最典型的事故（right hook）。转弯前一定要观察，自行车直行时要先让它过。": "A cyclist was catching up in the bike lane on your right. You didn't check the centre mirror, right mirror and right blind spot before turning, and cut right across the bike lane. This is the classic right-turn crash (the right hook). Always check before turning, and let a cyclist going straight go first.",
"你看到了右后方的自行车，但没有停下让它先过，就切进了自行车道。自行车在你右边直行时，右转车要让它先通过，再转。": "You saw the cyclist at your right rear but didn't stop to let it go first, and cut across the bike lane. When a cyclist is going straight on your right, a right-turning car must let it pass before turning.",
"灯已经变红，你的车停在人行横道外，没有占用人行横道，就应该停着等下一个绿灯。这时再转就成了“红灯右转”，要让横向的直行车和左边过来的行人，本练习不涉及，路考中这里不要抢着转。": "The light had already turned red and your car was stopped outside the crosswalk, not blocking it, so you should have stayed for the next green. Turning now would be a right turn on red, which must yield to cross traffic and to pedestrians from the left. This exercise doesn't cover that — on the road test, don't rush the turn here.",
"灯变黄时你还在停车线后，可以停下，你却继续开（或跟着前车转），变红灯后才越过停车线，这是闯红灯，路考直接不合格。黄灯亮时，能安全停下就要停在停车线后；前车过了线可以走，不代表你也可以跟着走。": "When the light turned amber you were still behind the stop line and could stop, but you kept going (or followed the car ahead) and crossed the line after it turned red. That is running a red light — an automatic fail. On amber, stop behind the line if you can do so safely; the car ahead getting through doesn't mean you can follow.",
"灯变黄时你还没到停车线，及时刹车是可以停在线后的，你却继续开过了停车线。快到路口时要一直留意信号灯，黄灯的意思是“停车，除非已经无法安全停下”。": "When the light turned amber you hadn't reached the stop line and could have braked in time to stop behind it, but you drove past the line. Keep watching the signal as you approach an intersection. Amber means stop, unless you can no longer stop safely.",
"灯变黄时你已经在路口里，对面等着的左转车会趁黄灯转弯。你应该继续停着，让它先转，然后马上跟着完成右转，两车不要同时进入路口。": "When the light turned amber you were already in the intersection, and the oncoming left-turner waiting there will turn on the amber. Stay stopped and let it turn first, then finish your right turn right after it. The two cars shouldn't enter at the same time.",
"你已经在路口里，让过左转车后应马上跟着完成转弯、离开路口，不要一直停在路口里。": "You are already in the intersection: after yielding to the left-turner, finish the turn right away and clear the intersection. Don't stay stopped there.",
"灯变黄时你已经越过停车线、但还没进入横向道路。对面在路口里等着的左转车会趁黄灯完成左转。你要先停车让它转过去，再尽快完成右转、离开路口。": "When the light turned amber you were past the stop line but not yet in the cross road. The oncoming left-turner waiting in the intersection will finish its turn on the amber. Stop and let it turn, then finish your right turn and clear the intersection as soon as you can.",
"灯变黄时你已经过了停车线，车头占用了人行横道。让过左转车后，虽然本方已经变红灯，也应该立刻完成转弯、离开人行横道。你一直停着，横向变绿灯后过马路的行人被你的车挡住了。": "When the light turned amber you were past the stop line with the front of the car in the crosswalk. After yielding to the left-turner, finish the turn right away and clear the crosswalk, even though your light is now red. You stayed stopped, and when the cross street turned green your car blocked the crossing pedestrians.",
"灯变黄后你的车头停在了人行横道上。让过对面左转车后，应该马上跟着完成转弯；你一直等到横向变绿灯、直行车开始走，这时已经走不了了，车还占着人行横道，挡住了横向过街的行人。": "After the light turned amber your car stopped with its front in the crosswalk. After yielding to the oncoming left-turner you should have finished the turn right away. You waited until the cross street turned green and its traffic started moving, so you couldn't go any more — and your car was still in the crosswalk, blocking crossing pedestrians.",
"灯变黄时你已经进入横向道路，应该继续完成转弯、尽快离开路口，不要停在路口里。": "When the light turned amber you were already in the cross road: keep going, finish the turn and clear the intersection quickly. Don't stop in the intersection.",
"听到警笛、看到闪灯的紧急车辆时，必须让路：安全的话靠边停车，未进入路口的车切勿进入路口，等它通过后再走。你在警车通过之前开进了路口，快到路口时听到警笛，要左右观察，找到它从哪里来。这是严重错误，路考直接不合格，警车已示意你靠边停车。": "When you hear a siren or see the flashing lights of an emergency vehicle, you must yield: pull over if it is safe, and if you haven't entered the intersection, don't enter it — wait until it has passed. You entered the intersection before the police car went through. When you hear a siren near an intersection, look left and right to find where it is coming from. This is a major error and an automatic fail — the police car has signalled you to pull over.",
"警车过去以后跟着转弯是可以的，但车头进入路口前要再按“观察路口”看一眼左边，确认后面没有别的紧急车辆。": "Turning after the police car has gone by is fine, but before the front of your car enters the intersection, press Check Intersection again to look left and make sure no other emergency vehicle is following.",
"你的车撞到了正在过马路的行人。转弯时一定要先让行人，看不清就停车等。": "Your car hit a pedestrian who was crossing the road. When turning, always yield to pedestrians first; if you can't see clearly, stop and wait.",
"右转前你没有做右后观察，没发现右边自行车道里的自行车，并入自行车道／转弯时把它撞倒了。转弯前一定要看中镜、右镜和右后盲区；发现自行车，就留在原车道，让它先过再转。": "You didn't check to your right rear before turning right, missed the cyclist in the bike lane on your right, and hit it while moving into the bike lane / turning. Always check the centre mirror, right mirror and right blind spot before turning; if there is a cyclist, stay in your lane and let it pass before turning.",
"你看到了右后方的自行车，却没有停车让它先过，把它撞倒了。自行车在你右边直行时，要等它过去再转。": "You saw the cyclist at your right rear but didn't stop to let it go first, and hit it. When a cyclist is going straight on your right, wait for it to pass before turning.",
"右转前一定要打右转灯，让后车、自行车和行人知道你要转。一般在停车线前约 30 米就打开。": "Always signal before a right turn so cars behind, cyclists and pedestrians know you are turning — usually about 30 m before the stop line.",
"你打了右转灯，但离停车线已经不到 15 米，后车、自行车和行人来不及反应。要更早打灯，一般在停车线前约 30 米就打开。": "You signalled right, but less than 15 m from the stop line — too late for cars behind, cyclists and pedestrians to react. Signal earlier, usually about 30 m before the stop line.",
"听到考官的指令后：看镜、打右转灯，再减速转进去，让后面的车早知道你要转。": "After the examiner's instruction: check the mirror, signal right, then slow down and turn in, so the cars behind know early that you are turning.",
"进停车场要横过人行道：有行人在走，停在人行道前面让他先过去。": "Entering the lot crosses a sidewalk: if a pedestrian is walking, stop before the sidewalk and let them cross first.",
"在停车场里转弯也要打灯：快到车道口时打好左转灯。": "Signal for turns in a parking lot too: put your left signal on as you approach the aisle.",
"对面开过来的车在通道上直行，你左转要横过它的车道：先停下让它过去，再转。": "An oncoming car is going straight along the aisle, and your left turn crosses its lane: stop and let it pass, then turn.",
"听到考官的指令后，减速之前先看后视镜（按住“左镜”看一眼后面有没有车跟着）。": "After the examiner's instruction, check the mirror before slowing down (hold Left Mirror to see whether a car is following).",
"要往左边的车位里停：减速之前打好左转灯，让后面和对面的车知道你要停进去。": "You are parking in a spot on the left: signal left before slowing down so the cars behind and ahead know you are pulling in.",
"往左转进车位之前要转头看左边（按住“看左边”）：车中间常有行人走出来，左边车道也可能有车。": "Before turning left into the spot, turn your head to look left (hold Look Left): pedestrians often step out from between cars, and there may be a car in the left lane.",
"这个项目要头进：车头朝里开进车位。": "This task is head-in parking: drive into the spot front first.",
"车身要全部停在车位的两条线中间，不能压到旁边的车位，车尾也不能留在车道上。": "The whole car must stop between the two lines of the spot — not over the next spot, and the rear must not stick out into the aisle.",
"停好后车身要在两条线中间，左右都要留出空间（旁边的车要能开门）。": "Once parked, the car should be between the two lines with room on both sides (so the cars beside you can open their doors).",
"停好后左右离两条线差不多远，旁边的车上下车才方便。": "Once parked, be about the same distance from both lines, so people in the cars beside you can get in and out easily.",
"停好后车身要和旁边的车平行（和车位线平行）。开进去时看到车身和车位线平行了，就回正方向盘，再直着往前开。": "Once parked, the car should be parallel to the cars beside it (and to the lines). As you drive in, straighten the wheel as soon as the car is parallel to the lines, then drive straight forward.",
"前面离路缘多远不好看，用两边的车来定：开到你的外后视镜和旁边车的外后视镜对齐（镜子对镜子），或者你和旁边车的司机位置对齐，就停。": "It's hard to judge how close you are to the curb ahead, so use the cars beside you: stop when your side mirror lines up with theirs (mirror to mirror), or your driver's seat lines up with theirs.",
"要开到底一点：车尾不要伸在车道上（车尾在车位线以内），车头也不要碰到前面的路缘。": "Pull far enough in: the rear must not stick out into the aisle (keep it inside the lines), and the front must not touch the curb ahead.",
"和车位线平行时就要回正方向盘，停好时车轮是正的。": "Straighten the wheel once you are parallel to the lines, so the wheels are straight when you stop.",
"开进去以后，往后倒、再往前算一次调整，最多两次。调整太多次，说明开始转的位置或打方向的时机不对。": "After you drive in, backing up and pulling forward again counts as one correction — two at most. Needing many corrections means you started turning at the wrong place or turned the wheel at the wrong time.",
"每次开始倒车之前，都要把四周看一遍（360° 观察），确认没有车、行人再倒。": "Before you start backing up each time, look all around (360° check) and make sure there are no cars or pedestrians.",
"车道上对面开过来的车离你很近时，不要把车头摆进它的车道：先停住让它过去，再转进车位。": "When an oncoming car in the aisle is close, don't swing your front into its lane: stop, let it pass, then turn into the spot.",
"停车的最后一步要挂 P，再拉手刹。": "The last step of parking is to shift to P, then set the parking brake.",
"放了锥桶的车位不能停。开进车位时看着两边的车和锥桶，慢慢开，随时准备停车。": "A spot with a traffic cone in it can't be used. Drive in slowly watching the cars and cones on both sides, ready to stop.",
"右转进考场之前要回头看右后方（右盲点）：右边可能有自行车或从后面上来的车。按“右后观察”。": "Before turning right into the test centre, look over your right shoulder (right blind spot): there may be a cyclist or a car coming up behind on your right. Press Look Back Right.",
"你右转、对面的车左转，进的是同一个口：右转车的路权比左转车高（左转车要让直行和右转的车），哪怕它先到、先在那里等。没有行人的话，应该直接转进去，不要停下来让它——停下让会让对方不知道该不该走，还会挡住后面的车。只有行人比你路权高。": "You are turning right and the oncoming car is turning left into the same entrance. A right-turner has priority over a left-turner (left-turners yield to through and right-turning traffic), even if it arrived first and is already waiting. With no pedestrians, turn in without stopping — stopping to yield leaves the other driver unsure whether to go and blocks the cars behind. Only pedestrians have priority over you here.",
"换线和进出口车道都要先打转向灯，让旁边车道和后面的车知道你要过去。": "Signal before every lane change and before moving into or out of the exit lane, so cars in the next lane and behind know you are coming over.",
"转向灯要提前打，至少闪 3 秒左右再换线（打灯、看后视镜、看盲点，做完正好 3 秒左右）。": "Signal early — let it flash for at least about 3 seconds before changing lanes (signal, mirror, blind spot takes about 3 seconds).",
"换线前要看中间后视镜和右边的外后视镜，看清后面和右边车道的车流。": "Before changing lanes, check the centre mirror and the right side mirror to see the traffic behind and in the right lane.",
"后视镜看不到车身右后方的盲区。换线、进入出口车道前一定要回头看一眼右边的盲点。": "The mirrors can't see the blind spot at your right rear. Always look over your right shoulder before changing lanes or moving into the exit lane.",
"看盲点要在动之前的最后一刻做，看完马上换线。隔了几秒，盲区里可能已经有车开进来了。": "Check the blind spot at the last moment before you move, and change lanes right after. A few seconds later a car may already have moved into the blind spot.",
"要过去的车道上有车和你并排或在你侧后方的盲区里，过去就会撞上它。确认旁边没车再动。": "A car was beside you or in the blind spot at your side rear in the lane you were moving into — you would hit it. Make sure the space beside you is clear before moving.",
"要过去的车道上，后面有车比你快、离你又不够远，你过去它就得刹车让你。要等它过去，或者等它离你足够远再动。": "A faster car was coming up behind in the lane you were moving into and wasn't far enough back — it would have to brake for you. Wait for it to pass, or until it is far enough back, before moving.",
"要过去的车道上，前面的车比你慢、离你太近。要等它和你拉开距离再过去。": "The car ahead in the lane you were moving into was slower than you and too close. Wait until there is more space before moving over.",
"看到出口预告牌（1 km）以后，就要找机会提早换到最右车道（出口专用道），不要拖到快到出口了还在主路车道上。": "After the exit advance sign (1 km), look for a chance to move into the rightmost lane (the exit lane) early — don't wait until you are almost at the exit and still on the main lanes.",
"出口减速车道从渐宽的地方（虚线开始）才有。之前右边是路肩，不能往右开。": "The exit deceleration lane only starts where the road widens (where the dashed line begins). Before that, the right side is the shoulder — don't drive onto it.",
"要提早按 后视镜 → 看盲点 → 换线 换进最右车道，这条车道前面直接分出去就是出口匝道。过了分岔口还在主路上，就只能开到下一个出口。": "Move into the rightmost lane early with mirror → blind spot → change lanes; that lane splits off ahead as the exit ramp. If you are still on the main road past the split, you have to go on to the next exit.",
"出高速要先换进最右的出口车道，快到出口时再在出口车道和匝道上减速。在主路上就减速，后面的车只能跟着急刹，非常危险。": "To leave the highway, first move into the rightmost exit lane, then slow down in the exit lane and on the ramp as you near the exit. Slowing on the main lanes forces the cars behind to brake hard — very dangerous.",
"出口匝道弯道的建议速度是 60 km/h。快到出口时就在出口车道里把车速降下来，进弯前降到 60 左右。": "The advisory speed for the exit ramp curve is 60 km/h. Slow down in the exit lane as you near the exit, to about 60 before the curve.",
"匝道尽头有停车标志（STOP），要在停车线前完全停住（车速为 0），再观察路口。": "There is a STOP sign at the end of the ramp: come to a complete stop (speed 0) at the stop line, then check the intersection.",
"要停在停车线后面、车头接近停车线的地方。停得太远，看不清路口的车，也容易让别人误会你的意图。": "Stop behind the stop line with the front of the car close to it. Stopping too far back, you can't see the traffic at the intersection, and others may misread what you intend to do.",
"高速上要和前车保持约 2 秒的距离。一直贴得很近（不到 0.7 秒，比如 100 km/h 时不到 20 米）就扣分。": "On the highway, keep about 2 seconds behind the car ahead. Staying very close (under 0.7 s — less than 20 m at 100 km/h) loses marks.",
"和前车的车速差太大、距离又近，只能急刹才不撞上。要提早松开加速、点减速。": "You were closing too fast on the car ahead and too close — only hard braking would avoid hitting it. Ease off the accelerator and slow down earlier.",
"换线前一定要看后视镜和回头看盲点，确认有足够的空档。": "Always check the mirror and look over your shoulder before changing lanes, to make sure there is a big enough gap.",
"这段高速限速 110，不要超过限速。": "The speed limit on this highway is 110 — don't go over it.",
"原来的车道车多才开 80；换进最右车道时离出口还很远，前面也没有慢车，应该跟上车流加速到 110 左右，快到出口（看到带箭头的 EXIT 牌）再减速。一直只开 80，后面的车只能跟着你或者急着超你。": "You only drove 80 because the old lane was busy. When you moved into the right lane the exit was still far away with no slow cars ahead, so you should have sped up with traffic to about 110, and slowed down only near the exit (when you see the EXIT sign with an arrow). Staying at 80 leaves the cars behind stuck behind you or rushing to pass.",
"匝道弯道建议 60 km/h。快到出口时就要在出口车道里把车速降下来，进弯前降到 60 左右。": "The ramp curve's advisory speed is 60 km/h. Slow down in the exit lane as you near the exit, to about 60 before the curve.",
"换线和并入高速都要先打转向灯（Signal），让旁边车道和后面的车知道你要过去，再看后视镜、回头看盲点，最后才动。": "Signal before every lane change and before merging onto the highway, so cars in the next lane and behind know you are coming over; then check the mirror and look over your shoulder, and only then move.",
"你要往哪边换线、并线，就打哪边的转向灯。": "Signal toward the side you are changing lanes or merging to.",
"转向灯要提前打，至少闪 3 秒左右再开始换线或并线，给别人反应的时间。": "Signal early — let it flash for at least about 3 seconds before you change lanes or merge, so others have time to react.",
"打灯后要看中间后视镜和要过去那一侧的外后视镜，看清后面和旁边车道的车流。": "After signalling, check the centre mirror and the side mirror on the side you are moving to, to see the traffic behind and beside you.",
"后视镜看不到车身侧后方的盲区。换线、并入高速前一定要回头看一眼要过去那一侧的盲点。": "The mirrors can't see the blind spot beside and behind the car. Always look over your shoulder on the side you are moving to before changing lanes or merging.",
"看盲点要在动之前的最后一刻做，看完马上换线（并线）。隔了几秒，盲区里可能已经有车开进来了。": "Check the blind spot at the last moment before you move, and change lanes (merge) right after. A few seconds later a car may already have moved into the blind spot.",
"完成换线、并入高速后要马上关掉转向灯（最晚 5 秒内）。": "Turn off the signal right after the lane change or merge (within 5 seconds at most).",
"去高速的匝道车道是右边多出来的那条车道。看到它出现后，要按 SMOG 尽早换进去；到了分岔口还在原来的车道，就错过了入口。": "The ramp lane to the highway is the extra lane that appears on the right. Once it appears, move into it early using SMOG; if you are still in your old lane at the split, you miss the entrance.",
"加速车道开头一段和高速之间是实线，不能并线。要开到虚线的地方，一边提速一边找空档再并入。": "At the start of the acceleration lane there is a solid line between it and the highway — no merging there. Drive on to the dashed section, speeding up and looking for a gap, then merge.",
"匝道弯道的建议速度是 50。弯道里可以慢慢提速，出弯看到加速车道以后再用力加速。": "The ramp curve's advisory speed is 50. Speed up gently in the curve, and accelerate hard once you are out of it and can see the acceleration lane.",
"右车道车很少、空档很大，也不能一到虚线就慢慢并进去。要在加速车道里先把车速加到限速 110 左右，再并入。": "Even with light traffic and big gaps in the right lane, don't drift in slowly as soon as the line turns dashed. Speed up to about the 110 limit in the acceleration lane first, then merge.",
"右车道车多、车流约 85 时，并入时车速要接近车流。为了让开旁边的车先减一点速没问题，但并进去的时候要已经加回来（低于约 72 就太慢），不然后面的车只能急刹。": "With heavy traffic in the right lane moving at about 85, merge at close to traffic speed. Slowing a little to let a car beside you go first is fine, but be back up to speed when you merge (below about 72 is too slow), or the cars behind have to brake hard.",
"加速车道最后一段慢慢收窄，在这里并线是可以的，但车身不能越过右边的白线进到路肩。走到收窄段还没并进去，就要尽快找空档并线，不要让车被挤到线外。": "The last part of the acceleration lane narrows. Merging here is fine, but don't cross the white line on the right onto the shoulder. If you reach the taper without merging, find a gap and merge quickly — don't get squeezed off the lane.",
"高速车流约 110，并入后要保持在限速附近，跟上车流。": "Highway traffic flows at about 110. After merging, keep near the speed limit and keep up with traffic.",
"并入后要和前车拉开安全距离（理想是 2 秒左右）。刚并进去时近一点可以，但几秒内要松开加速或点减速，把距离拉开；一直贴得很近（不到 0.7 秒，比如 100 km/h 时不到 20 米）就扣分。": "After merging, open up a safe gap to the car ahead (ideally about 2 seconds). Being a little close right after merging is OK, but within a few seconds ease off or slow down to open the gap; staying very close (under 0.7 s — less than 20 m at 100 km/h) loses marks.",
"比车流快很多并入不是问题，前提是前面的空档够大。如果并进去以后要急刹才不撞前车，说明速度太快或空档太小。": "Merging much faster than traffic is fine as long as the gap ahead is big enough. If you have to brake hard after merging to avoid the car ahead, you were too fast or the gap was too small.",
"加速车道约 380 米，要一边提速一边看后视镜和盲点，看到合适的空档就果断并入。走到尽头只能停车，非常危险。": "The acceleration lane is about 380 m. Speed up while checking the mirror and blind spot, and merge decisively when you see a suitable gap. Reaching the end means stopping — very dangerous.",
"换线、并线前一定要看后视镜和回头看盲点，确认有足够的空档。": "Always check the mirror and look over your shoulder before changing lanes or merging, to make sure there is a big enough gap.",
"这段高速限速 110。并入以后跟上车流就可以，不要超过限速。": "The speed limit on this highway is 110. After merging, just keep up with traffic — don't go over the limit.",
"听到指令后，先打右转灯、做右侧观察，再踩刹车靠边。": "After the instruction: signal right and do a right-side check first, then brake and pull over.",
"靠边、离开之前都要先看后视镜（左侧观察、右侧观察里都有）。": "Check the mirror before pulling over and before pulling away (it is part of both the left-side and right-side checks).",
"踩刹车靠边之前，要做右侧观察：中镜、右镜、右盲点。": "Before braking to pull over, do a right-side check: centre mirror, right mirror, right blind spot.",
"从路边开出来之前，要打左转灯、做左侧观察，确认安全再走。": "Before pulling away from the curb, signal left and do a left-side check; go only when it's safe.",
"从路边开出来之前，要做左侧观察（中镜、左镜、左盲点）：后面可能有车正要开过来。": "Before pulling away from the curb, do a left-side check (centre mirror, left mirror, left blind spot): a car may be coming up from behind.",
"要停在离路缘（或路边）30 厘米以内（45 厘米内不算错），车身和路边平行。": "Stop within 30 cm of the curb (or road edge) — within 45 cm is not an error — with the car parallel to it.",
"停车时车身要和路边平行，车头不要歪着。": "When parking, keep the car parallel to the road edge — don't leave the front angled.",
"上坡有路缘：方向盘往左打（车轮朝外），松刹车后车往后溜，前轮抵住路缘；下坡有路缘、没有路缘：方向盘往右打（车轮朝路边）。": "Uphill with a curb: turn the wheel left (wheels away from the curb) so that when you release the brake the car rolls back and the front wheel rests against the curb. Downhill with a curb, or no curb: turn the wheel right (wheels toward the road edge).",
"停坡道时方向盘要打到底（或接近打到底），车万一滑动才能被路缘挡住、或者往路边走。": "When parking on a hill, turn the wheel all the way (or nearly), so that if the car rolls, the curb stops it or it rolls toward the road edge.",
"有路缘：方向打好、挂 N，点一下松刹车，让车轻轻溜到车轮抵住路缘，停稳后再挂 P。": "With a curb: turn the wheel, shift to N, release the brake briefly and let the car roll gently until the wheel rests against the curb; once it is still, shift to P.",
"车轮方向不对，松开刹车后车往路中间溜。坡道停车要先把车轮转对方向，再松刹车。": "The wheels were turned the wrong way, so the car rolled toward the middle of the road when you released the brake. On a hill, turn the wheels the right way first, then release the brake.",
"停车的最后一步要挂 P（再熄火、拉手刹）。": "The last step of parking is to shift to P (then turn off the engine and set the parking brake).",
"换线要先打转向灯（Signal），让旁边车道和后面的车知道你要过去，再看后视镜、回头看盲区，最后才换线。": "Signal before changing lanes so cars in the next lane and behind know you are coming over, then check the mirror and look over your shoulder, and only then change lanes.",
"你要往哪边换线，就打哪边的转向灯。": "Signal toward the side you are changing lanes to.",
"转向灯要提前打，至少闪 3 秒左右（三四下）再开始换线，给别人反应的时间。打灯后马上就换，等于没打。": "Signal early — let it flash for at least about 3 seconds (three or four flashes) before changing lanes, so others have time to react. Changing right after signalling is as good as not signalling.",
"打灯后要先看中间后视镜和要换过去那一侧的外后视镜（Mirror），看清后面和旁边车道的车流。": "After signalling, check the centre mirror and the side mirror on the side you are moving to (Mirror), to see the traffic behind and beside you.",
"后视镜看不到车身侧后方的盲区。换线前一定要回头（Over shoulder）看一眼要换过去那一侧的盲区，确认没有车。": "The mirrors can't see the blind spot beside and behind the car. Before changing lanes, always look over your shoulder (Over shoulder) on the side you are moving to and make sure it is clear.",
"回头看盲区要在换线前的最后一刻做，看完马上换。隔了几秒，盲区里可能已经有车开进来了。": "Look over your shoulder at the last moment before changing lanes, and change right after. A few seconds later a car may already have moved into the blind spot.",
"换线那一刻，要换过去的车道上有车和你并排或在你侧后方的盲区里，换过去会撞上它。看后视镜、回头看盲点，确认旁边没有车再换。": "At the moment you changed lanes, a car was beside you or in the blind spot at your side rear in that lane — you would hit it. Check the mirror and look over your shoulder, and make sure the space beside you is clear before changing.",
"要换过去的车道上，后面有车比你快、离你又不够远，你换过去它就得刹车让你。要等它过去，或者等它离你足够远（换过去以后它不用刹车）再换。": "A faster car was coming up behind in the lane you were moving into and wasn't far enough back — it would have to brake for you. Wait for it to pass, or until it is far enough back (so it won't need to brake after you move over).",
"要换过去的车道上，前面的车比你慢、离你太近，换过去你就贴在它后面。要等它和你拉开距离再换。": "The car ahead in the lane you were moving into was slower than you and too close, so you'd end up right behind it. Wait until there is more space before changing.",
"换线完成后要马上关掉转向灯（最晚 5 秒内），否则别人会以为你还要换线或转弯。": "Turn the signal off right after the lane change (within 5 seconds at most), or others will think you are about to change lanes or turn again.",
"考官要求换线后，要在安全的时候尽快完成。空档不够可以等，但看到足够的空档就要果断换过去。": "After the examiner asks for a lane change, complete it as soon as it is safe. You can wait if the gap is too small, but when you see a big enough gap, move over decisively.",
"换线前一定要看后视镜和回头看盲区，确认旁边车道有足够的空档。": "Always check the mirror and look over your shoulder before changing lanes, to make sure the next lane has a big enough gap.",
"车没动的时候不要转方向盘：伤轮胎和转向系统，路考会扣分。要先让车慢慢动起来，再一边走一边打方向。": "Don't turn the steering wheel while the car is stopped: it wears the tires and steering, and loses marks on the road test. Get the car rolling slowly first, then steer as it moves.",
"换挡（D、R、P）之前要先把车完全停住。": "Bring the car to a complete stop before shifting (D, R, P).",
"停车的最后一步：挂 P 以后，还要拉上手刹（点 P 档左边的手刹键）。": "Last step of parking: after shifting to P, also set the parking brake (the brake button to the left of P).",
"倒车时要回头从后窗看后面（按住“回头看”），不能只看后视镜。": "When backing up, turn and look through the rear window (hold Look Back) — don't rely only on the mirrors.",
"靠近路缘时要很慢，车轮最多轻轻碰到路缘，不能撞上去。": "Go very slowly near the curb: the wheels may at most touch it gently — don't hit it.",
"车轮压上路缘、人行道，在路考里是严重错误。": "Driving a wheel up onto the curb or sidewalk is a major error on the road test.",
"倒车、转弯时车身四个角都要留意，随时准备停车。": "When backing and turning, watch all four corners of the car and be ready to stop.",
"听到考官的指令后，在减速之前先看后视镜（后面有没有车、离多近），再打转向灯。": "After the examiner's instruction, check the mirror (is there a car behind, and how close) before slowing down, then signal.",
"要靠边停车：先看后视镜、打右转灯，再减速，让后面的车早点知道你要停。": "To pull over: check the mirror, signal right, then slow down, so the car behind knows early that you are stopping.",
"听到指令后要提早、平稳地减速。刹得太急，后面的车来不及反应。": "After the instruction, slow down early and smoothly. Braking too hard leaves the car behind no time to react.",
"听到考官指令后要提早减速，在指定的位置停下来。开过头了在路考里就是没有完成这个项目。": "After the examiner's instruction, slow down early and stop at the place you were told. Overshooting means you didn't complete the task on the road test.",
"靠边停车不能挡住别人家的车道（车道口那一段路缘是平的）。要停在两个车道口中间的路边。": "When pulling over, don't block someone's driveway (where the curb is flat). Stop at the curb between two driveways.",
"没有路缘的路边，车轮不要开出路边白线、开到砂石路肩外面去。": "Where there is no curb, don't let the wheels go past the white edge line onto the gravel shoulder.",
"你的车停在了人行横道上，行人只能绕着你的车走，这是严重错误。停车时不应占用人行横道。": "Your car stopped on the crosswalk, so pedestrians had to walk around it — a major error. Never stop on a crosswalk.",
"从对面走来的行人还在人行横道上（或正要踏上），你就转弯了。对面来的行人要等他们完全走完人行横道再转。": "Pedestrians coming from the far side were still on the crosswalk (or about to step onto it) when you turned. Wait until pedestrians from the far side have completely finished crossing before turning.",
"从你身后一侧来、要直行过街的行人，还没走过道路一半，你就转弯了。需要等他们走过一半以上才可以转；转弯前要看右后方。": "Pedestrians coming from behind you on your side, going straight across, had not yet crossed half the road when you turned. Wait until they are more than halfway across before turning, and check your right rear before turning.",
"你停车让行以后，绿灯下再起步前没有再按“右后观察”。停车等待期间，后面可能又有行人或自行车过来，每次重新起步前都要再看一遍中镜、右镜和右后盲区。": "After stopping to yield, you didn't press Look Back Right again before moving off on the green. While you were waiting, more pedestrians or cyclists may have come up behind; every time you move off again, check the centre mirror, right mirror and right rear blind spot again.",
"车头进入右侧人行横道之前，要再做一次右后观察（中镜、右镜、右后盲区），确认没有行人、自行车从右后方过来。": "Before the front of your car enters the crosswalk on the right, do another right-rear check (centre mirror, right mirror, right rear blind spot) to make sure no pedestrian or cyclist is coming from behind on the right.",
"平行停车之前：看后视镜、打右转灯（告诉后面的车你要停车）、看右边盲点。": "Before parallel parking: check the mirror, signal right (to tell the car behind you are stopping), and check the right blind spot.",
"开到参考车旁边停车之前，要先看后视镜，确认后面没有车紧跟着。": "Before stopping beside the reference car, check the mirror first to make sure no car is following closely behind.",
"平行停车倒进去之前，要回头看右边盲点：右后方可能有自行车、行人。": "Before backing into the parallel spot, look over your right shoulder: there may be a cyclist or pedestrian behind you on the right.",
"起始位置：和参考车平行、相隔约 1 米，你的后保险杠和它的后保险杠对齐（或者你的后轮对准它的车尾）。": "Starting position: parallel to the reference car, about 1 m away, with your rear bumper lined up with its rear bumper (or your rear wheels lined up with its back end).",
"车要停进两辆车之间的车位里，车身全在路边，不能停在车道上。": "Park in the space between the two cars, with the whole car at the curb — not in the traffic lane.",
"平行停车最后要离路缘 30 厘米以内（前后轮都在 45 厘米内不算错）。": "Finish parallel parking within 30 cm of the curb (both front and rear wheels within 45 cm is not an error).",
"平行停车最后要离路缘 30 厘米以内，这次稍远了一点（前后轮都在 45 厘米内不算错）。": "Finish parallel parking within 30 cm of the curb — this time you were a little farther (both front and rear wheels within 45 cm is not an error).",
"停好后车身要和路缘平行：前轮、后轮离路缘差不多远。差得多，就再往前或往后调整一下。": "Once parked, the car should be parallel to the curb: front and rear wheels about the same distance from it. If they differ a lot, pull forward or back to adjust.",
"停好后前后都要留出空间：挂 D 往前一点，停在两辆车中间（能看到前车的后轮落地处）。": "Once parked, leave space in front and behind: shift to D, pull forward a little, and stop between the two cars (where you can see where the car ahead's rear wheels meet the ground).",
"倒进去以后，往前、再往后算一次调整，最多两次（最后往前停到中间不另算）。调整太多次，说明打方向的时机不对。": "After backing in, one forward-and-back counts as one correction — two at most (the final pull forward to the middle doesn't count). Needing many corrections means you turned the wheel at the wrong time.",
"每次开始倒车之前，都要把四周看一遍（360° 观察：左后盲点、左镜、中镜、右镜、右后盲点、正后面），确认没有车、自行车、行人再倒。": "Before you start backing up each time, look all around (360° check: left rear blind spot, left mirror, centre mirror, right mirror, right rear blind spot, straight back) and make sure there are no cars, cyclists or pedestrians.",
"平行停车要一直观察四周：倒车前做一次 360° 观察，车身斜着回正时再做一次，往左打方向前再做一次（至少 3 次）。": "Keep checking all around while parallel parking: a 360° check before backing, again as you straighten from the angle, and again before turning the wheel left (at least 3 times).",
"倒车、打方向时车头会摆到车道上。发现后面有自行车过来，要停车让它先过去，再继续。": "When you back and turn, the front of the car swings out into the lane. If you see a cyclist coming from behind, stop and let it pass, then continue.",
"这次你的车正好停着，自行车过去了，但它过来之前你没有观察（360° 观察、左镜）。倒车时要一直观察四周。": "This time your car happened to be stopped when the cyclist passed, but you hadn't checked (360° check, left mirror) before it came. Keep checking all around while backing.",
"停好车的最后一步要挂 P（再熄火、拉手刹）。": "The last step of parking is to shift to P (then turn off the engine and set the parking brake).",
"红灯右转前，必须在停车线后完全停住（车速为 0），然后再观察、再转。慢慢滑过停车线不算停车，路考直接不合格。": "Before turning right on red, you must come to a complete stop (speed 0) behind the stop line, then check and turn. Rolling slowly over the line is not a stop — an automatic fail.",
"你转弯时，横向有直行车正开过来或已经在路口里。红灯右转要让横向的车：两条车道都要看，左道（内道）的车虽然不会和你进同一条车道，也不能和它同时进入路口。要等到明显的空档再转。": "When you turned, cross traffic was coming or already in the intersection. A right turn on red must yield to cross traffic: watch both lanes. Even though a car in the left (inner) lane won't end up in your lane, don't enter the intersection at the same time as it. Wait for a clear gap before turning.",
"你车头前的人行横道上有行人在过街（横向是绿灯，他们有路权），你就开了过去。要等行人走过你的车头、离开你的路线再走。": "Pedestrians were crossing the crosswalk in front of you (the cross street has a green and they have the right-of-way) and you drove through. Wait until the pedestrians have passed your front and are out of your path before going.",
"横向自行车道里有自行车从左边骑过来，你转弯时挡住了它的路。自行车和直行车一样，要让它先过。": "A cyclist was coming from the left in the cross street's bike lane, and your turn blocked its way. Treat a cyclist like through traffic — let it go first.",
"你的车和其他车辆撞上了。没有让行、抢着进路口，就会造成碰撞，路考立即结束。": "Your car collided with another vehicle. Not yielding and forcing your way into the intersection causes collisions — the road test ends immediately.",
"你的车撞到了横向骑过来的自行车。": "Your car hit a cyclist coming along the cross street.",
"红灯右转前，最危险的车和人都从左边来。车头进入路口前，要按“观察路口”看左边（两条车道和人行横道），确认没有车和人再走。": "Before a right turn on red, the most dangerous cars and people come from the left. Before the front of the car enters the intersection, press Check Intersection to look left (both lanes and the crosswalk) and make sure it is clear before going.",
"左边停着一辆高大的 SUV，挡住了你看横向车流的视线。在停车线停稳后，应该按“行驶”慢慢往前挪（随时准备按停车），挪到能看清左边的位置再按“观察路口”，不能只在 SUV 后面看一眼就转。": "A tall SUV parked on the left was blocking your view of cross traffic. After stopping fully at the stop line, press Drive to creep forward (ready to press Stop) until you can see to the left, then press Check Intersection. Don't turn after just one look from behind the SUV.",
"按 G 路考的要求，红灯右转时，车头进入右侧人行横道之前要做一次右后观察，确认右后方没有自行车或行人。": "For the G road test, on a right turn on red, do a right-rear check before the front of the car enters the crosswalk on the right, to make sure there is no cyclist or pedestrian behind you on the right.",
"红灯右转第一次停车，应该停在停车线后面。你停过了线（还没到人行横道），完全停车是做到了，但位置不对。": "On a right turn on red, your first stop should be behind the stop line. You stopped past the line (before the crosswalk) — a full stop, but in the wrong place.",
"红灯右转应该先在停车线后停稳，再慢慢往前挪出来观察。你一次就停到了人行横道上，完全停车是做到了，但位置不对；如果这时有行人过街，就是挡住行人的严重错误。": "On a right turn on red, first stop fully behind the stop line, then creep forward to look. You stopped on the crosswalk in one go — a full stop, but in the wrong place; if pedestrians were crossing at that moment, it would be a major error for blocking them.",
"你的车停在人行横道上，挡住了正在过街的行人，他们只能绕着你的车走。没有行人时，车头可以挪到人行横道上观察；有行人时，车头要停在人行横道前。": "Your car stopped on the crosswalk and blocked pedestrians who were crossing, so they had to walk around it. With no pedestrians, you may creep onto the crosswalk to look; with pedestrians, stop before the crosswalk.",
"对面亮起左转箭头绿灯时（有时只有对面亮，你这边一直是红灯，看不到箭头，但能看到对面左转车开始转），对面左转车有优先权。你还是红灯，红灯右转要等左转车转完、或者出现明显的空档再转；左转车已经在转、或者马上就要开出来时，不能进入路口。": "When the oncoming side gets a green left-turn arrow (sometimes only the other side gets it — your light stays red and you can't see the arrow, but you can see the oncoming left-turners start to turn), those left-turners have priority. You still have a red light: a right turn on red must wait until they have turned or there is a clear gap. Don't enter the intersection when a left-turner is turning or about to come through.",
"右转前一定要打右转灯，一般在停车线前约 30 米就打开。": "Always signal before a right turn, usually about 30 m before the stop line.",
"离停车线不到 15 米才打右转灯，后车和行人来不及反应。": "You signalled right less than 15 m from the stop line — too late for the cars behind and pedestrians to react.",
"先要靠右边停车：看后视镜、打右转灯、回头看右边盲点，再慢慢靠过去。": "First pull over to the right: check the mirror, signal right, look over your right shoulder, then move over slowly.",
"每次起步、换方向之前都要先看后视镜。": "Check the mirror every time before moving off or changing direction.",
"靠右边停车前，要回头看右边盲点。": "Look over your right shoulder before pulling over to the right.",
"三点调头要先停在离右边路缘 30 厘米以内，路面才够用。": "For a three-point turn, first stop within 30 cm of the right curb so you have enough road to use.",
"第一步往前左转之前，要打左转灯、看后视镜、回头看左边盲点。": "Before the first step (forward and left), signal left, check the mirror and look over your left shoulder.",
"第一步往前左转之前，一定要回头看左边盲点：后面可能有车正开过来。": "Before the first step (forward and left), always look over your left shoulder: a car may be coming up from behind.",
"三点调头之前要做 360° 观察：路上两个方向的车、自行车、行人都要确认没有。": "Before a three-point turn, do a 360° check: make sure there are no cars, cyclists or pedestrians in either direction.",
"倒车之前要做 360° 观察（四周看一遍，包括正后面），确认没有车、自行车、行人再倒。": "Before backing up, do a 360° check (look all around, including straight back) and make sure there are no cars, cyclists or pedestrians.",
"第二步倒车之前，按 M.S.B.：看后视镜、打右转灯、回头看。": "Before the second step (backing up), do M.S.B.: mirror, signal right, look back.",
"最后一步往前开之前，看后视镜、打左转灯、看盲点，再开走。": "Before the last step (forward), check the mirror, signal left, check the blind spot, then drive off.",
"往前、倒车都要在碰到路缘之前停住。": "Stop before touching the curb, both going forward and backing up.",
"三点调头要在三步（前、后、前）内完成。每一步方向盘要打得够快、够多，到路中间开始回方向盘，停在路缘前。": "Finish the three-point turn in three steps (forward, back, forward). Turn the wheel quickly and fully at each step, start straightening at the middle of the road, and stop before the curb.",
"调头之前和调头过程中要一直观察两边：有车开过来，要停下来让它先过。": "Keep watching both ways before and during the turn: if a car comes, stop and let it pass.",
"调过头以后要开在新方向的右边车道（原来的对面车道）。": "After turning around, drive in the right lane for the new direction (what was the oncoming lane).",
"这个项目要尾进：车尾朝里倒进车位，车头朝着车道。": "This task is reverse parking: back into the spot rear first, with the front facing the aisle.",
"车身要全部停在车位的两条线中间，不能压到旁边的车位，车头也不能伸到车道上。": "The whole car must stop between the two lines of the spot — not over the next spot, and the front must not stick out into the aisle.",
"停好后车身要和旁边的车平行（和车位线平行）。倒车时看到车身和旁边的车平行了，就把方向盘回正，再直着往后倒。": "Once parked, the car should be parallel to the cars beside it (and to the lines). When the car becomes parallel to the cars beside you while backing, straighten the wheel and back straight in.",
"后面离路缘多远不好看，要用两边的车来定：倒到你的外后视镜和旁边车的外后视镜对齐（镜子对镜子），或者你和旁边车的司机位置对齐，就停。": "It's hard to judge how close you are to the curb behind, so use the cars beside you: stop when your side mirror lines up with theirs (mirror to mirror), or your driver's seat lines up with theirs.",
"要倒到底一点：车头不要伸到车道上（车头在车位线以内），车尾也不要碰到后面的路缘。": "Back far enough in: the front must not stick out into the aisle (keep it inside the lines), and the rear must not touch the curb behind.",
"和旁边的车平行时就要回正方向盘（Straighten），停好时车轮是正的。": "Straighten the wheel (Straighten) as soon as you are parallel to the cars beside you, so the wheels are straight when you stop.",
"倒进去以后，往前、再往后算一次调整，最多两次。调整太多次，说明起始位置或打方向的时机不对。": "After backing in, one forward-and-back counts as one correction — two at most. Needing many corrections means your starting position or the timing of your steering was off.",
"每次开始倒车之前，都要把四周看一遍（360° 观察：左后盲点、左镜、中镜、右镜、右后盲点、正后面），确认没有车、行人再倒。": "Before you start backing up each time, look all around (360° check: left rear blind spot, left mirror, centre mirror, right mirror, right rear blind spot, straight back) and make sure there are no cars or pedestrians.",
"停车场的车道上有车开过来时，先停住让它过去，再倒车。你一动，车头就会摆到车道上挡住它。": "When a car is coming along the aisle, stop and let it pass before backing up. As soon as you move, your front swings out into the aisle and blocks it.",
"这次你正好停着，那辆车过去了，但它过来之前你没有观察（360° 观察、左镜）。倒车前和倒车时要一直观察四周。": "This time you happened to be stopped when that car passed, but you hadn't checked (360° check, left mirror) before it came. Keep checking all around before and while backing.",
"停好车的最后一步要挂 P，再拉手刹。": "The last step of parking is to shift to P, then set the parking brake.",
"放了锥桶的车位不能停。倒车时看着两边的车和锥桶，慢慢倒，随时准备停车。": "A spot with a traffic cone in it can't be used. Back in slowly watching the cars and cones on both sides, ready to stop.",
"四面停牌（ALL WAY）路口：谁先完全停稳谁先走。别的车比你先停下，要等它先通过（离开路口）再走；同时停下时让右边的车。": "At an all-way stop (ALL WAY), whoever comes to a full stop first goes first. If another car stopped before you, wait until it has gone through (left the intersection); if you stop at the same time, yield to the car on your right.",
"在路口直行不要打转向灯，不然别人会以为你要转弯。": "Don't signal when going straight through an intersection, or others will think you are turning.",
"四面停牌路口，前面先到的车都走了、轮到你时，要果断开过去。等太久，别的车会以为你在让它，反而更乱。": "At an all-way stop, when the cars that arrived before you have gone and it's your turn, go decisively. Waiting too long makes others think you are yielding to them, which only causes confusion.",
"到停牌路口前（约 30 米）就要打左转灯，停车、观察、转弯的整个过程都开着。": "Signal left before reaching the stop sign (about 30 m before), and keep it on through the stop, the check and the turn.",
"左转灯要在停车之前就打好（离路口约 30 米），让后面和对面的人早知道你要左转。": "Put the left signal on before you stop (about 30 m before the intersection), so the people behind and ahead know early that you are turning left.",
"停牌路口必须完全停住（车速为 0）；没有停车线时，停在人行横道前。慢慢滑过去（rolling stop）在路考里是严重错误。": "You must come to a complete stop (speed 0) at a stop sign; if there is no stop line, stop before the crosswalk. Rolling through (a rolling stop) is a major error on the road test.",
"没有停车线时，要停在人行横道前面，车头不要压到人行横道。": "If there is no stop line, stop before the crosswalk — don't let the front of the car go onto it.",
"车头要停在接近人行横道的地方（1～2 米内）。停得太远看不清路口，之后还要再往前挪。": "Stop with the front of the car close to the crosswalk (within 1–2 m). Stopping too far back, you can't see the intersection and will have to creep forward again.",
"停稳以后、起步左转之前，要看左边、看右边（最好再看一眼左边），两个方向的来车都要看清。": "After stopping and before moving off to turn left, look left, look right (ideally left again once more), and see the traffic both ways clearly.",
"路角的树和灌木挡住视线时，要先在人行横道前完全停车；没有行人时，再慢慢往前挪（前移）到能看清两边来车的地方（不能进入横路），停下来再看左、看右，确认安全再转。": "When trees and bushes at the corner block your view, first stop fully before the crosswalk; if there are no pedestrians, creep forward slowly (Creep) until you can see traffic both ways (without entering the cross street), stop, look left and right again, and turn when it is safe.",
"行人在人行横道上（或正要走上来）时，车要停在人行横道前，等他完全走过马路、走上对面的人行道，才能往前挪或转弯。": "When a pedestrian is on the crosswalk (or about to step onto it), stop before the crosswalk and wait until they have completely crossed and reached the far sidewalk before creeping forward or turning.",
"横路的车不用停，你要让它。左边的车离你太近时转弯，你会挡在它前面，逼它急刹，甚至撞上。": "Cross traffic doesn't have to stop — you must yield to it. Turning when a car from the left is too close puts you in front of it, forcing it to brake hard or even crash.",
"你要转进去的那条车道上，右边来的车不用停。它离得太近时转进去，它只能急刹或撞上你。": "Cars from the right in the lane you are turning into don't have to stop. Turning in when one is too close forces it to brake hard or hit you.",
"两边都没车、看得也清楚的时候，要果断转弯。等了很久不走，会影响后面的车，也算犹豫不决。": "When there are no cars either way and you can see clearly, turn decisively. Waiting a long time holds up the cars behind and counts as hesitation.",
"你这条路没有停牌，对面的直行车也不停：左转要让它。离得太近（几秒内就到路口）时转过去，会挡在它前面，逼它急刹甚至撞上。要等它过去、或者等到足够大的空档再转。": "Your road has no stop sign, and oncoming through traffic doesn't stop either: a left turn must yield to it. Turning when it is too close (a few seconds from the intersection) puts you in front of it, forcing it to brake hard or even crash. Wait for it to pass, or for a big enough gap.",
"没有停牌的路口左转：转之前要看清对面的来车、你要转进去那条路上的行人（看左），也要看一眼右边。": "Left turn at an intersection without a stop sign: before turning, check the oncoming traffic and the pedestrians on the road you are turning into (look left), and take a look to the right too.",
"横路有停牌、你这条路没有：停牌后的车必须让你，哪怕你是左转、它是直行。对面没车、没有行人时，应该直接转，不要停下来等它——你停下让它，它不知道该不该走，后面的车也被你挡住。": "The cross street has a stop sign and your road doesn't: cars at the stop sign must yield to you, even when you are turning left and they are going straight. With no oncoming cars and no pedestrians, turn without stopping to wait for them — if you stop to yield, they won't know whether to go, and you block the cars behind.",
"没有停牌、对面也没有来车的时候，要果断左转。停在路口等太久，后面的车会被你挡住，也算犹豫不决。": "With no stop sign and no oncoming traffic, turn left decisively. Waiting too long in the intersection blocks the cars behind and counts as hesitation.",
"左转要让横路两个方向的车。看不清就慢慢前移再看，确认两边都有足够的空档再走。": "A left turn must yield to cross traffic both ways. If you can't see clearly, creep forward and look again; go only when both directions have a big enough gap.",
"直行通过路口也要知道后面的情况：开始接近路口时（离路口 100 多米），要看一眼中镜。万一前面有情况要急刹，你也知道后车离你多近。": "Going straight through an intersection, you still need to know what's behind you: as you start to approach (100-plus metres before it), glance at the centre mirror. If you have to brake hard for something ahead, you'll know how close the car behind is.",
"绿灯直行也要观察路口：车头进入路口前（离路口几十米时），按“观察路口”左右看，确认横向没有闯红灯的车、没有还在过街的行人。": "Check the intersection on a green light too: before the front of the car enters (a few dozen metres before), press Check Intersection to look left and right and make sure no cross traffic is running the red and no pedestrians are still crossing.",
"开过路口以后要再看一次中镜，掌握后面车流的情况。红灯后起步的，在加速到 60 的过程中看。": "After going through the intersection, check the centre mirror again to keep track of the traffic behind. If you started from a red light, do it while speeding up to 60.",
"这段路限速 60。超过限速会扣分；按住减速把车速降回 60 左右。": "The speed limit here is 60. Going over it loses marks — hold Slow Down to bring your speed back to about 60.",
"这段路限速 60，车流也在 60 左右。没有原因开得太慢（低于约 50），会妨碍后面的车。": "The speed limit here is 60 and traffic is moving at about 60. Driving too slowly without a reason (below about 50) holds up the cars behind.",
"和前车至少保持 2 秒左右：前车经过一个路标，你数“一千零一、一千零二”再经过。太近时松开加速或按一下减速。": "Keep at least about 2 seconds behind the car ahead: when it passes a landmark, count \"one thousand and one, one thousand and two\" before you pass it. If you are too close, ease off the accelerator or tap Slow Down.",
"你的车和别的车撞上了。看到前车刹车灯亮、前面是红灯，要提前按住减速。": "Your car collided with another car. When you see the brake lights of the car ahead or a red light ahead, hold Slow Down early.",
"看到前面红灯、前车刹车，开始减速的时候要看一眼中镜，知道后车离你多近、有没有跟得太紧。": "When you see a red light ahead or the car ahead braking, glance at the centre mirror as you start to slow down, so you know how close the car behind is and whether it is following too closely.",
"停在前车后面，要停在能看到前车后轮和地面接触的地方（从驾驶座看，前车车尾下面的路面要露出来，大约留 4～6 米）。停得太近，前车溜车或出故障时，你没有余地绕开。": "When stopping behind another car, stop where you can see its rear tires touching the road (from the driver's seat, the road under its back end should be visible — about 4–6 m). Stopping too close leaves you no room to get around it if it rolls back or breaks down.",
"停在前车后面，能看到它的后轮和地面就可以了（大约 4～6 米），不要留出两个车身那么大的空当。": "When stopping behind another car, it's enough to see its rear tires and the road (about 4–6 m) — don't leave a gap of two car lengths.",
"在红灯前停稳以后，要再看一次中镜，看后面的车有没有停稳、会不会追尾。": "After stopping at the red light, check the centre mirror again to see whether the car behind has stopped and won't rear-end you.",
"红灯时车头越过了停车线。": "The front of your car crossed the stop line on a red light.",
"变绿灯、前车开走以后，你过了很久才起步，妨碍后面的车。": "After the light turned green and the car ahead moved off, you waited a long time before going, holding up the cars behind.",
"过了路口要平稳地加速到 60 左右，开得太慢会妨碍后面的车。": "After the intersection, speed up smoothly to about 60; driving too slowly holds up the cars behind."
});
function TT(s){return EN&&TTD[s]||s}
if(EN){
 const tr=s=>{const k=s.trim();if(!k||!/[一-龥]/.test(k))return null;if(TTD[k])return s.replace(k,TTD[k]);
  const q=k.match(/^这一趟有 (\d+) 处需要注意：$/);const c=k.match(/^(.+?)(（[^（）]*）)$/);if(c&&TTD[c[1]]){const w=c[2].match(/^（进弯时 (\d+) km\/h）$/);const t2=TTD[c[2]]||(w?'(entered the curve at '+w[1]+' km/h)':null);if(t2)return s.replace(k,TTD[c[1]]+' '+t2)}if(q)return s.replace(k,q[1]+(q[1]==='1'?' thing':' things')+' to work on this run:');const m=k.match(/^(左|右) (\d+°)( 到底)?$/);if(m)return(m[1]==='左'?'L ':'R ')+m[2]+(m[3]?' full lock':'');return null};
 const SEL='button,button span,#rot,#rot div,#rot a,#hud,#wtx,.pz,.pz p,#fl,small,a.back,#ov h2,#ov p,#ov .card b,#ov .card span,#ov .mu';      /* #ov：总结卡片 */
 // 按钮里的小字可能分成几行（<br>），合起来查表
 const fixEl=el=>{if(el.tagName==='SMALL'){const t=el.textContent.trim(),v=t&&TTD[t];if(v&&el.textContent!==v)el.textContent=v;return}
  let hit=false;el.childNodes.forEach(n=>{if(n.nodeType===3){const v=tr(n.nodeValue);if(v!=null&&v!==n.nodeValue){n.nodeValue=v;hit=true}}});
  if(hit&&el.tagName==='BUTTON')el.querySelectorAll('small').forEach(x=>{if(!/[一-龥]/.test(x.textContent))x.style.display='none'})};      /* 按钮换成英文以后，原来的英文小字（如 Signal）就重复了，藏起来 */
 const run=root=>{const r=root&&root.nodeType===1?root:document.body;if(!r)return;if(r.matches&&r.matches(SEL))fixEl(r);r.querySelectorAll(SEL).forEach(fixEl);
  const p=r.closest&&r.closest(SEL);if(p&&p!==r)fixEl(p)};
 // 英文比中文长：按钮里放不下时，把按钮的字（连同小字）一起慢慢缩小，直到放得下（最小约 6 成）
 const fit=x=>{if(!x||x.tagName!=='BUTTON'||!x.classList.contains('b')||!x.offsetWidth)return;const key=x.textContent+'|'+x.clientWidth+'x'+x.clientHeight;if(x.dataset.fk===key&&x.scrollWidth<=x.clientWidth+1&&x.scrollHeight<=x.clientHeight+1)return;      /* 按钮内容被重写（小字没了缩小的样式）时也要重新算 */
  x.style.fontSize='';const sm=[...x.querySelectorAll('small')];sm.forEach(e=>e.style.fontSize='');
  const f0=parseFloat(getComputedStyle(x).fontSize),s0=sm.map(e=>parseFloat(getComputedStyle(e).fontSize)),ov=()=>x.scrollWidth>x.clientWidth+1||x.scrollHeight>x.clientHeight+1;
  for(let r=.94;ov()&&r>=.58;r-=.06){x.style.fontSize=(f0*r).toFixed(1)+'px';sm.forEach((e,i)=>e.style.fontSize=Math.max(8.5,s0[i]*r).toFixed(1)+'px')}
  x.dataset.fk=x.textContent+'|'+x.clientWidth+'x'+x.clientHeight};
 const fitAll=()=>document.querySelectorAll('button.b').forEach(fit);let fq=0;const sched=()=>{if(!fq)fq=requestAnimationFrame(()=>{fq=0;fitAll()})};
 addEventListener('resize',()=>setTimeout(fitAll,120));
 const go=()=>{document.documentElement.lang='en';run(document.body);fitAll();
  new MutationObserver(ms=>{let k=false;ms.forEach(m=>{if(m.type==='attributes'&&m.attributeName==='style'&&m.target.tagName==='BUTTON'&&m.oldValue&&/display/.test(m.oldValue+m.target.getAttribute('style')))k=true});if(k)sched()}).observe(document.body,{attributes:true,attributeFilter:['style'],attributeOldValue:true,subtree:true});
  new MutationObserver(ms=>{let q=0;ms.forEach(m=>{const t=m.target.nodeType===1?m.target:m.target.parentElement;if(t){run(t);if(t.closest&&t.closest('button.b'))q=1}});if(q)sched()}).observe(document.body,{childList:true,subtree:true,characterData:true})};
 if(document.body)go();else addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',go)}
